---
import {mediaUrl} from '../data/brain/teaching-library';
const views=[{id:'duomo',name:'Face the Duomo'},{id:'away',name:'Face away'},{id:'compare',name:'Compare reports'}];
---
<section class="guitar-learning" data-representational-neglect aria-label="Imagined viewpoint and reported landmarks">
  <div class="guitar-actions"><div><h2>Change the imagined viewpoint</h2><p>Compare the reports while the square stays fixed.</p></div><div class="guitar-buttons">{views.map((view,i)=><button type="button" data-viewpoint={view.id} aria-pressed={i===0}>{view.name}</button>)}</div></div>
  <div class="learning-screen" data-square-scenes>
    {views.map((view,i)=><img data-square-scene={view.id} src={mediaUrl(`interaction-neglect-${view.id}.png`,'l14')} width="1280" height="720" alt={view.id==='duomo'?'Facing the Duomo: patients report buildings on their imagined right and omit those on their imagined left.':view.id==='away'?'Facing away: previously omitted buildings are now reported. The new imagined left is omitted.':'Both imagined reports together show that the spatial knowledge remains available; access changes with attention.'} hidden={i!==0} />)}
  </div>
  <div class="learning-controls"><button type="button" data-square-reset>↺ Reset</button><button type="button" data-illustration-fullscreen>⛶ Fullscreen</button></div>
  <p class="learning-limit">Bisiach &amp; Luzzatti’s two patients. The original illustrations show reported imagined scenes; omission does not mean erased memory.</p>
</section>
<style>
  [data-square-scenes]{background:#fcfcf9}[data-square-scene]{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;animation:scene-in .35s ease-out}[data-square-scene][hidden]{display:none}[data-viewpoint][aria-pressed=true]{border-color:#c8ba88;background:#35392c}@keyframes scene-in{from{opacity:0}to{opacity:1}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){[data-square-scene]{animation:none}}
</style>
